# Lyra beta tester quick run (device-backed)

python3 scripts/ops/lyra_beta_trainer.py --serial <DEVICE_SERIAL>

Manual verification focus for this adjustment:
1. Open Scan results.
2. Tap `Start incident`.
3. Confirm Incident assistant opens as a separate page (not layered over scan-results content).
4. Confirm `Back to scan results` returns cleanly.
5. Tap `Apply fix for me` and confirm the app first asks `Apply recommended best settings?`.
6. On Apply path, confirm recommended auto actions run first and uninstall/containment can still be offered for high-risk incidents.
7. If prompted, confirm Android permission request appears before recommended auto actions (Wi-Fi posture cases).
8. Tap `Guide me step-by-step` and confirm the same recommended-settings decision appears first.
9. On Guide path, confirm manual recommended-settings guidance appears before full step-by-step flow.
10. Confirm manual dialog shows `Path pack:` with device-specific wording (MIUI/Samsung One UI/Google Pixel/Generic Android).
11. Confirm `Open with overlay guide` is shown; if overlay permission is off, verify permission prompt appears.
12. After granting overlay permission the first time, confirm flow returns to the manual dialog and lets user tap `Open with overlay guide` again (no dead-end).
13. Confirm compact overlay guide shows one current target at a time and includes an in-place `Hide` link that collapses the card while keeping the tap target readable; tap `Show` to restore `Previous`, `Done this step`, and `Finish guide`. On Samsung/MIUI secure screens, verify fallback still works if overlay is temporarily hidden.
14. Confirm tap text is explicit for OEM path:
    - Xiaomi/MIUI uses `App permissions` and `Other permissions`.
    - Samsung/Pixel uses `Permissions` and special access rows.
15. Confirm risky permission wording is explicit (`Camera`, `Microphone`, `Location`, `Contacts`, `Phone`, `SMS`, `Files/Media`) instead of generic "risky permissions".
16. In Incident assistant, tap `Skip for now` and confirm it advances to the next unresolved incident when available.
17. Verify `Work on this now` uses the same app identity standard for high/medium/low incidents:
    compact app icon + bold common app name (when package metadata is present).
18. Open Credential Defense Center and confirm the guided foundation dialog exposes `Open with overlay guide` and `Open settings now`.
19. Confirm the adaptive foundation overlay stays retail-safe in this phase: deterministic local rule packs remain the controller, manual anchor confirmation remains available, `Analyze current screen` is user-triggered only, OCR runs on-device, there is no screenshot upload, no continuous capture, no Accessibility capture, and no autonomous taps.
20. Confirm the overlay asks `What do you see?`, shows anchor buttons that match the visible screen, and only updates after the tester taps a matching anchor. Use `Analyze current screen` and confirm it asks for screen-capture consent, returns `Detected: ...`, `Possible matches: ...`, or `No reliable match found`, and still leaves manual anchor buttons available. Use `Reset route` and confirm the flow returns to the first state.
21. On Xiaomi/MIUI, confirm autofill guidance explicitly warns that search can dead-end on `Accounts & sync` / `Android Auto`, routes first through `Passwords & accounts > Autofill service > Google`, and if Xiaomi redirects into Google services uses `Google Password Manager` or `Autofill with Google` as the fallback route. Confirm the final return step points to `Recheck now`, not `Scan breaches`.
22. Confirm returning from Credential Defense settings with saved adaptive progress shows the last guided step context and offers `Resume last guided step`, `Restart guided route`, and `Open Settings again`.
23. Confirm `Restart guided route` clears the saved adaptive session and starts the flow from the first step.
24. Confirm successful foundation completion clears the saved adaptive session instead of leaving stale resume data behind.
